{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The Elohim before whom my fathers walked.</b> He did not wish to include himself and say 'the Elohim whom I and my fathers walked before,' for he did not wish to regard himself as a perfect righteous person; and whoever is not a perfect righteous person should not say 'before Him,' but rather 'with Him,' for he needs support to sustain him — like Noah, of whom it is said, ״אֶת הָאֱלֹהִים הִתְהַלֶּךְ נֹחַ״ (Genesis 6:9). And he mentioned 'the Elohim' twice, and the third time he mentioned 'the angel,' because the first two are not fit except for HaShem alone: for walking before Elohim means the divine service, as its Targum renders: ״דִּי פְלַחוּ אֲבָהָתַי קֳדָמוֹהִי״ — 'whom my fathers served before Him.' And likewise, 'the Eloim who has been my shepherd from my youth' means sustenance, for it is among the four keys that were not given to an intermediary. And the seekers of remgez said that 'מֵעוֹדִי' (from my youth) has the numerical value of one hundred and thirty — namely those one hundred and thirty years that HaShem sustained him before he came to Egypt. 'עַד הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה' (until this day): the word 'הַזֶּה' (this) has the numerical value of seventeen — namely those seventeen years that he lived in Egypt. And this means: even though it appeared as though Joseph sustained him those seventeen years, nevertheless he attributes them to those one hundred and thirty years — just as those were surely from HaShem, so too these seventeen years. But concerning the matter of protection from all evil, which is done through an intermediary, he said, 'the angel who redeems me from all evil,' for always ״מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה לִשְׁמָרְךָ בְּכָל דְּרָכֶיךָ״ — 'He will give His angels charge over you, to guard you in all your ways.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:13.063238435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}